{title: Whiskey in the Jar}
{artist: Traditional Irish}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, irish, pub}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As [G]I was a-goin' [G]over the far-famed [Em]Kerry [Em]mountains
I [C]met with Captain [C]Farrell and his [G]money he was [G]countin'
I [G]first produced my [G]pistol and I [Em]then produced my [Em]rapier
Saying [C]"Stand and de[C]liver, for you [G]are a bold de[G]ceiver!"

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Musha ring dum a doo dum a [D]da
[G]Whack for my daddy-o, [C]whack for my daddy-o
[G]There's whiskey [D]in the [G]jar [G]

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [G]counted out his [G]money and it [Em]made a pretty [Em]penny
I [C]put it in my [C]pocket and I [G]took it home to [G]Jenny
She [G]sighed and she [G]swore that she [Em]never would de[Em]ceive me
But the [C]devil take the [C]women, for they [G]never can be [G]easy
